
Hello from Canada(near Vancouver) Rick, I just wanted to let you know I
downloaded your Euchre game from Aminet earlier this evening, and I'd like
to thank you for your programming efforts! :)

I've always enjoyed playing Euchre, and your program is something that(at
least in my opinion), the Amiga has been lacking, i.e. one of the *great*
card games.

Unfortunately, playing on a computer doesn't quite provide the enjoyment of
playing with/against three other people, but when you don't have three
others around, your game will make a good substitute, on occasion.

As with all new programs, there are a few things that seem to need ironing
out:

1.) The trump suit, displayed on the top, left, of the screen after a
couple of tricks, is partially missing.

2.) I've played a couple of games, and have yet to see the score! The word
"Score" is on the screen, and after every hand, the score seems to be
displayed *extremely* briefly, but it's way too fast to read.

3.) A suggestion here - possibly the trump suit, the score, *and* the
number of tricks(us vs. them) could all be displayed in the same area of
the screen.... possibly along the bottom. That way all the information
would be in one place.

4.) Another suggestion - if possible, the font should be larger, and
thicker, to make the game info easier to read. I do have a 17" monitor, but
when I start getting tired that puny font just doesn't cut it.

5.) And just one more suggestion, although I'm not sure if this one will
make it better or not - it might make the game slightly easier to play, if
the cards in the middle, as they're played, were all facing up for the game
player to read them easier. It's still pretty good the way it is, but I
*think* it may be a bit better this way.

Once again, thanks for your programming efforts, and I hope you keep up the
good work! :)

